## Lane Detection

| User intent | Lane |
|-------------|------|
| Ask, tell, talk, consult, research, explain, how-to | Advisory |
| Add, build, create, implement, develop, feature, make | Mission |
| Fix, debug, diagnose, broken, error, bug, crash, investigate | Debug |
| Edit prompt, config, doc, small fix, human already made changes, just commit | Quick |

## Cursor Mode Bridge

| User intent | Lane | Cursor mode / action |
|---|---|---|
| Ask / explain | Advisory | Ask Mode (or Agent, no writes) |
| Roadmap work | Mission | Agent + `/sc-run` |
| Bug hunt | Debug | Cursor Debug Mode |
| Ship | Ship | Agent + `/sc-ship` |
| Small edit / commit | Quick | Agent (no full mission gates) |

After clarify clear, prefer `/sc-run`; no non-blocking questions mid-AFK. Ship only via `/sc-ship`. Detail: `.cursor/skills/sc-run`, `sc-ship`, `sc-mission`.

## AFK flow

```
clarify (human) → [/sc-run UI draft HIL if visual] → /sc-run build → human check → /sc-ship
```

`/sc-run` build: jigsaw plan tasks → per-acceptance RED (sc-tester) → GREEN (sc-coder) with auto checkpoint commits → combine/refactor + integration gate → review → `ready`. For visual UI/FE: stop after draft HTML (layout/style/components) until human approves; after build, require screenshots/visual verify + functional tests before `ready`. `/sc-ship` squashes checkpoints to ≤5 commits, then merges.

`spacecraft map use|current|next` select and advance the roadmap.

## Roadmap / issues

- Large work (>7 tasks): `spacecraft map new`, then add missions; AFK with `/sc-run`.
- Bug radar any lane: `gh issue create` + record in mission `issues.md` / roadmap `issues`.
- Fix issue #N: view issue → mission → reference in spec → close after ship.

## Mission resolution

Branch `feat/<id>/…` → `.space/missions/<id>/mission.json`. List: `ls .space/missions/`. State: `spacecraft set-state [id] <state>` (`state` alias). CLI: `evidence`/`evi`, `validate`/`val`, `roadmap`/`map`.

Clarify status: `open` | `clear` | `deferred` under mission dir.

## Lanes (pointers)

- **Mission:** `/sc-run` (plan/build/review via agents). Detail: `sc-mission`, `sc-planning`, `sc-tdd`, `sc-verification`.
- **Ship:** `/sc-ship` - validate, rebase, merge `--no-ff`, archive.
- **Quick:** skips spec/plan/TDD/formal review; still git safety + tests; report ready, wait for ship.
- **Debug:** reproduce E2E → falsify root cause → record in `issues.md`. Prefer Cursor Debug Mode for runtime evidence.

## Subagent Delegation

Orchestrator, not implementer. Task-delegate:

| Agent | Role |
|---|---|
| `sc-coder` | production code |
| `sc-tester` | tests + evidence |
| `sc-planner` | plan.json |
| `sc-reviewer` | release readiness |
| `sc-designer` | UI critique |
| `sc-adviser` | complex design |
| `sc-firmware` | STM32 C |

Patterns: UI draft HTML before visual FE code; tester before coder (one acceptance per pair); firmware for embedded; refactor after all slices; UI visual + functional recheck; reviewer before ship.

## Session Handoff

Unfinished work: state, blockers, dirty git, next pickup. End with recommended next action.
